<h1>Linking to Limpidity</h1>

<p><img src="img/lpdtnow.gif" width="88" height="31" alt="Limpidity Now! button" /></p>

</div>

<p>It's easy. Just download the button to your web site and
use the following HTML code:</p>

<div class="codeblock">
&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.limpidity.com&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;lpdtnow.gif&quot; width=&quot;88&quot; height=&quot;31&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;
alt=&quot;Limpidity Now!&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
</div>

<p>Feel free to customize the HTML code to suit your web page but please
do not alter the button image itself. You may need to add a path or location
before the button's file name.</p>

<p>I also have a somewhat larger link button:</p>

<p align="center"><img src="img/limpiditylogo.jpg" width="206" height="153" alt="Limpidity Logo" /></p>

<p>The HTML code for that is as follows:</p>

<div class="codeblock">

&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.limpidity.com&quot;&gt;
